+# Agent 10 carry-observability computations
+
+These exact finite controls accompany the independently checked Lean sources. They are computational evidence, not substitutes for the actual-history inclusion theorems or kernel certificates. Sources and JSON outputs are retained byte-for-byte from the Agent 10 semantic specialist's work.
+
+## Scope of each calculation
+
+| Files | Complete finite domain | Result |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `witness_scan.cpp`, `witness_scan.json` | All 4,504,864 ordered admissible width-eleven word pairs with difference `[1,-3,5,-6,6,-6,6,-6,5,-3,1]` | 89 pairs survive six complete observations; none survive seven or eight. Swapping the pair covers the negated difference. |
+| `prefix_scan.py`, `prefix_scan.json` | All 272 valid two-column starts with difference `(1,-3)`, every shared Boolean inner-carry path through the requested horizon | The weak necessary graph has survivor counts `202,119,60,35,14,5,0` after observations one through seven. The separate Lean certificate checks the exclusion and the actual-history theorem justifies its use. |
+| `replay_numeric.py`, `replay_numeric.json` | The two ordinary integers `80000571539` and `70000817069`, observations zero through seven | Direct decimal reversal/addition confirms six equal complete carry words, then separation. `Agent10SixCarryCounterexample.lean` separately proves the actual numeric certificate. |
+| `padded_witness_scan.cpp`, `padded_witness_scan.json` | All admissible width-thirteen pairs with the once-padded difference `[0,1,-3,5,-6,6,-6,6,-6,5,-3,1,0]`, after a complete necessary eight-observation prefix filter | No pair survives eight complete observations. The prefilter domain has 85,857,408 pairs; all 324 possible initial two-column pairs are checked. Thirty surviving weak prefixes yield 7,949,760 fully enumerated completions. |
+
+The width-thirteen search uses the weak prefix filter whose actual-history inclusion is proved in `Agent10PrefixExclusion.actual_history_survives`. It also reports a stronger filter for comparison, but does not use that stronger filter to discard enumerated completions.
+
+The width-thirteen survivor counts after the eight-observation filter and zero through eight additional complete-word checks are `[7949760,528456,111213,69129,15194,5592,734,0,0]`. The zero at seven is conditional on the eight-observation prefilter. It does **not** prove that no unrestricted width-thirteen pair with this difference survives seven observations. The complete conclusion of that search is the absence of an eight-observation pair in the stated width-thirteen domain.
+
+The ordinary example's shared actual inner-bit path is `[0,0,1,1,0,0]`. A prefix BFS can display a different valid path, including an all-zero path, from the same initial outer states. An abstract path and its particular whole-word realization must not be conflated.
+
+## Three-column extension
+
+`three_prefix_scan.py` and `three_prefix_scan.json` compare three necessary relations over all 5,184 valid starts with difference `(0,1,-3)`. All three low carries are observed. The relation formalized in `Agent10ThreeColumnExclusion` observes the terminal high carry and the high carry at `L-1`; its survivor counts through eight observations are `[3870,2355,1345,774,413,160,42,0]`. The terminal-only relation leaves thirteen starts at eight; observing all three high carries yields the stronger counts `[3870,2346,1246,692,334,134,37,0]`. These are distinct relations.
+
+Run `python -B three_prefix_scan.py` to reproduce that JSON. The final Lean source checks the finite exclusion using a proved base-19 state encoding, then transports actual histories through valid states.
+
+## Reproduce without overwriting retained results
+
+The Python programs print JSON to standard output. The C++ programs use integer arithmetic and assertions; compile with assertions enabled.
+
+```bash
+python -B prefix_scan.py > /tmp/agent10-prefix-replay.json
+python -B replay_numeric.py > /tmp/agent10-numeric-replay.json
+c++ -std=c++17 -O2 witness_scan.cpp -o /tmp/agent10-witness-scan
+/tmp/agent10-witness-scan > /tmp/agent10-witness-replay.json
+c++ -std=c++17 -O2 padded_witness_scan.cpp -o /tmp/agent10-padded-scan
+/tmp/agent10-padded-scan > /tmp/agent10-padded-replay.json
+```
+
+These controls make no claim about arbitrary widths, arbitrary coefficient differences, seven-observation optimality, or an infinite ordinary-integer trajectory. The separate source/evidence manifest records exact hashes of the programs and outputs.
diff --git a/calculation/agent10-carry-observability-20261016/padded_witness_scan.cpp b/calculation/agent10-carry-observability-20261016/padded_witness_scan.cpp
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..47c52c98
--- /dev/null
+++ b/calculation/agent10-carry-observability-20261016/padded_witness_scan.cpp
@@ -0,0 +1,142 @@
+#include <algorithm>
+#include <array>
+#include <cassert>
+#include <cstdint>
+#include <iostream>
+#include <map>
+#include <string>
+#include <utility>
+#include <vector>
+
+// Exact, exhaustive once-padded search. Width is 13, difference is
+// [0,1,-3,5,-6,6,-6,6,-6,5,-3,1,0], and observations are t=0,...,7.
+// Swapping the two words covers the opposite sign.
+//
+// Filter completeness: Agent10PrefixExclusion.actual_history_survives maps
+// every actual complete eight-word agreement into the WEAK shared-bit prefix
+// graph used below. All 324 possible initial prefixes are tested. The weaker
+// graph is used for enumeration even though the stronger necessary graph
+// leaves only six starts. No successful prefix is skipped or sampled.
+using Word=std::vector<int>;
+using Prefix=std::pair<int,int>;
+constexpr int width=13;
+const Word difference{0,1,-3,5,-6,6,-6,6,-6,5,-3,1,0};
+std::array<std::uint64_t,9> survived{};
+std::map<std::string,std::uint64_t> full_patterns;
+std::vector<std::pair<Word,Word>> examples;
+std::vector<Prefix> weak_prefixes,strong_prefixes;
+
+std::array<int,4> observe(Prefix state,int e) {
+  int p=state.first,q=state.second;
+  int a=p/10,b=(q+a)/10,u=(q+e)/10,h=(p+u)/10;
+  return {a,b,u,h};
+}
+Prefix next_prefix(Prefix state,int e) {
+  int p=state.first,q=state.second;
+  auto [a,b,u,h]=observe(state,e);
+  Prefix result=h==0 ? Prefix{2*p+u-10*a,2*q+a+e-10*(b+u)}
+                    : Prefix{p-10*a+1,p+q+a+u-10*(b+h)};
+  assert(1<=result.first && result.first<=18);
+  assert(0<=result.second && result.second<=18);
+  return result;
+}
+bool prefix_survives(int n,Prefix q,Prefix r,bool strong) {
+  if(n==0)return true;
+  for(int e=0;e<2;++e) {
+    auto a=observe(q,e),b=observe(r,e);
+    bool match=strong ? a==b : a[0]==b[0] && a[1]==b[1] && a[3]==b[3];
+    if(match && prefix_survives(n-1,next_prefix(q,e),next_prefix(r,e),strong))return true;
+  }
+  return false;
+}
+bool admissible(const Word& q) {
+  if(q.empty() || q.front()==0)return false;
+  for(std::size_t i=0;i<q.size();++i) {
+    if(q[i]<0 || q[i]>18 || q[i]!=q[q.size()-1-i])return false;
+    if(i==q.size()-1-i && q[i]%2!=0)return false;
+  }
+  return true;
+}
+Word carries(const Word& q) {
+  Word c(q.size()+1,0);
+  for(std::size_t i=0;i<q.size();++i)c[i+1]=(q[i]+c[i])/10;
+  return c;
+}
+Word next_pairs(const Word& q,const Word& c) {
+  Word d;
+  for(std::size_t i=0;i<q.size();++i)d.push_back((q[i]+c[i])%10);
+  if(c.back())d.push_back(c.back());
+  Word result(d.size());
+  for(std::size_t i=0;i<d.size();++i)result[i]=d[i]+d[d.size()-1-i];
+  assert(admissible(result));
+  return result;
+}
+void inspect(const Word& r) {
+  Word q(width);
+  for(int i=0;i<width;++i)q[i]=r[i]+difference[i];
+  assert(admissible(q) && admissible(r));
+  ++survived[0];
+  Word a=q,b=r;
+  std::string pattern;
+  for(int t=0;t<8;++t) {
+    Word ca=carries(a),cb=carries(b);
+    if(ca!=cb)return;
+    ++survived[t+1];
+    pattern.push_back(ca.back() ? 'O':'N');
+    if(t!=7) { a=next_pairs(a,ca); b=next_pairs(b,cb); }
+  }
+  assert(prefix_survives(8,{q[0],q[1]},{r[0],r[1]},true));
+  ++full_patterns[pattern];
+  if(examples.size()<5)examples.push_back({q,r});
+}
+void complete(Word& r,int i) {
+  if(i==7) { inspect(r);return; }
+  int lo=std::max(0,-difference[i]);
+  int hi=std::min(18,18-difference[i]);
+  for(int v=lo;v<=hi;++v) {
+    if(i==6 && v%2!=0)continue;
+    r[i]=r[width-1-i]=v;
+    complete(r,i+1);
+  }
+}
+void print_word(const Word& q) {
+  std::cout<<'[';
+  for(std::size_t i=0;i<q.size();++i){if(i)std::cout<<',';std::cout<<q[i];}
+  std::cout<<']';
+}
+void print_prefixes(const std::vector<Prefix>& ps) {
+  std::cout<<'[';
+  bool first=true;
+  for(auto [p,q]:ps){if(!first)std::cout<<',';first=false;std::cout<<'['<<p<<','<<q<<']';}
+  std::cout<<']';
+}
+int main() {
+  for(int p=1;p<=18;++p)for(int q=0;q<=17;++q) {
+    if(prefix_survives(8,{p,q+1},{p,q},true))strong_prefixes.push_back({p,q});
+    if(!prefix_survives(8,{p,q+1},{p,q},false))continue;
+    weak_prefixes.push_back({p,q});
+    Word r(width);
+    r[0]=r[12]=p;r[1]=r[11]=q;
+    complete(r,2);
+  }
+  assert(weak_prefixes.size()==30 && strong_prefixes.size()==6);
+  assert(survived[0]==7949760);
+  std::cout<<"{\n  \"width\":13,\n  \"difference\":";print_word(difference);
+  std::cout<<",\n  \"complete_words_requested\":8,\n  \"all_admissible_candidates_before_filter\":85857408,";
+  std::cout<<"\n  \"prefix_filter\":\"weak shared-bit graph, identical to compiled actual_history_survives\",";
+  std::cout<<"\n  \"prefix_pairs_checked\":324,\n  \"weak_surviving_r_prefixes\":";print_prefixes(weak_prefixes);
+  std::cout<<",\n  \"strong_surviving_r_prefixes\":";print_prefixes(strong_prefixes);
+  std::cout<<",\n  \"survivors_after_prefix_filter_and_n_complete_words\":[";
+  for(int i=0;i<=8;++i){if(i)std::cout<<',';std::cout<<survived[i];}
+  std::cout<<"],\n  \"eight_word_overflow_patterns\":{";
+  bool first=true;
+  for(const auto& [k,v]:full_patterns){if(!first)std::cout<<',';first=false;std::cout<<'"'<<k<<"\":"<<v;}
+  std::cout<<"},\n  \"eight_word_examples\":[";
+  first=true;
+  for(const auto& [q,r]:examples){
+    if(!first)std::cout<<',';
+    first=false;
+    std::cout<<"{\"q\":";print_word(q);std::cout<<",\"r\":";print_word(r);std::cout<<'}';
+  }
+  std::cout<<"]\n}\n";
+}
